<task id="151" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>#1038 hardening — RecordContainerResolver must normalize aliases and REFUSE entity names that are not real Dataverse logical names, instead of reading an unrecognised name as "not securable"</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-30, session 27; owner round 2 item 7)</phase>
    <gate>blocked until PR #1045 (word-add-in-r1) is merged to master AND master is merged into this branch — it introduces `DocumentAssociationMap.ToLogicalName` and the OfficeService caller fix this task builds on.</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Security-path .cs change in the SPE container-isolation seam (tags bff-api, auth, security).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Changes the fail-closed contract of the one component that decides whether secure content can land in a shared, non-retractable SPE container; every upload path in the BFF depends on it.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Independent of 144 and 145 (no shared files). Shares Infrastructure/Dataverse/RecordContainerResolver.cs with task 133 (C11 — rewrites the fail-closed log/detail route text at `:250-254`) and task 150 (ABSENT branch `:211-227`; 150 depends on this task). Sequencing: 151 before 150; 151 and 133 not concurrently — whichever lands second rebases (disjoint regions, trivial). SystemCacheKeys.cs is read (not modified) by task 132.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none inside this project; external gate PR #1045 (see gate). Sequenced before 150; not concurrent with 133.</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, dataverse, cache, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>GitHub #1038 (word-add-in-r1, found by its task 080 review) + owner round 2 item 7 ("#1038: yes, harden the resolver"). Caller audit on master 2026-09-30 in the session-27 orchestration.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>RecordContainerResolver answers "which container does this record's content belong in?". Today it lowercases whatever entity name it is given and asks the securable-entity registry; a name the registry does not recognise is treated as "cannot be secure" and the content is routed to a non-secure container. That is how an Office save to a secure project, passed as the friendly name "project", landed in the shared container (#1038). Make the resolver itself refuse to guess: map known aliases to their logical names, and refuse any name that is not a real entity.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer — BFF SPE container-isolation seam. Fail closed (ADR-003); an unknown answer is never "not secure".</role>

  <goal>`RecordContainerResolver.ResolveForRecordAsync` (both overloads) (a) maps every alias in `DocumentAssociationMap` to its logical name before any decision, (b) resolves a real non-securable entity exactly as today, (c) resolves a real securable entity exactly as today, and (d) throws a typed `SdapProblemException` for a name that is neither an alias nor a real Dataverse entity logical name — never returning a non-secure decision for it. The OBO record-keyed upload routes give a correct answer for alias names instead of a misleading 409. Guards prove each branch bites.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>THE FAIL-OPEN, AT ITS ROOT. `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Dataverse/RecordContainerResolver.cs:138-155`: the name is only trimmed and lower-cased (`:143`), then `if (!await _securableEntities.IsSecurableAsync(normalizedEntity, ct))` returns `SecureContainerDecision.Decide(isSecure: false, …)` (`:151-155`). `SecurableEntityRegistry.IsSecurableAsync` (`SecurableEntityRegistry.cs:61-70`) answers `Contains(name)` over the set of entities carrying `sprk_issecure` — so "project", a misspelling, or any non-entity string is indistinguishable from "a real entity that cannot be secure". The registry's own metadata query already enumerates EVERY entity in the org (the entity query is unfiltered; entities without the attribute come back with an empty attribute collection — `SecurableEntityRegistry.cs:114-173`, note at `:157-162`), so the knowledge needed to tell "unknown" from "not securable" is fetched and thrown away.

#1038 (OPEN): `OfficeService.ResolveContainerAsync` passed the friendly type from `POST /api/office/save` straight in. On THIS branch it still does (`Services/Office/OfficeService.cs:228`); on the peer branch it maps through `DocumentAssociationMap.ToLogicalName(target.EntityType) ?? target.EntityType` first (PR #1045, `OfficeService.cs:243` there). Note the `?? target.EntityType`: an unmapped name still reaches the resolver raw, which is why the resolver itself must refuse.

`DocumentAssociationMap.ToLogicalName` is introduced by PR #1045 (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs:112-142` on branch work/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1): matter, project, invoice, workassignment, event, todo (friendly and logical) and contact. It is NOT on master or this branch yet (master has only `TryApply`, `Models.cs:86`).

CALLER AUDIT (this branch, 2026-09-30):
- `Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:598` — literal "sprk_project". Safe.
- `Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs:1394-1396` — `ComposeHostEntityLogicalName` = "sprk_matter" (`:1207`). Safe.
- `Services/Communication/Engine/CommunicationContainerResolver.cs:101-103` — names come from the communication's securable regardings (Dataverse-sourced, `:146-180`). Safe.
- `Api/OBOEndpoints.cs:119` and `:363` — ROUTE-SUPPLIED `{entityLogicalName}`. The route filter authorizes aliases (`RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter` via `EntityAccessFilter.TryResolveEntitySet`, alias map at `Api/Filters/EntityAccessFilter.cs:108-147` accepts "project", "matter", …), then the resolver sees "project", reads it as non-securable with no fallback, and the handler returns 409 "No storage container is configured" (`OBOEndpoints.cs:121-135`). Fails closed, but the message is wrong — and a non-secure project named by alias is refused although its business-unit container is derivable.
- `Services/Office/OfficeService.cs:228` — the #1038 fail-open caller (fixed on the peer branch).
No caller today legitimately passes a name that is not a real entity.</background>
