  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: RecordContainerResolver.ResolveForRecordAsync (both overloads). A name that is neither a `DocumentAssociationMap` alias nor a real entity logical name throws a typed `SdapProblemException` (a new stable code, e.g. `container_entity_unknown`); it never returns a decision. A metadata failure while deciding "is this a real entity" propagates (same contract as `IsSecurableAsync` today) — it is not read as "unknown" or "not securable".</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: the "real entity" knowledge. Extend `ISecurableEntityRegistry` / `SecurableEntityRegistry` to retain the entity names its existing metadata query already returns; do NOT add a second metadata service, a second metadata round trip, or a hard-coded entity list. Alias mapping uses `DocumentAssociationMap.ToLogicalName` — do not copy its table.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-009 / NFR-08">Scope: caching. The known-entity set is cached with the same 6h TTL, never cached when empty, and under a key that is allow-listed in `SystemCacheKeys.cs` with its system-level justification. A cached value written by the PREVIOUS build (securable names only) must never be read as the known-entity set — change the key or version it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: behaviour preservation. For every real logical name, the decision is byte-for-byte what it is today (secure → own container or 409 fail-closed; non-secure → caller fallback or owning-BU container). Only unknown names and aliases change behaviour.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: OBOEndpoints record-keyed routes. The authorization key and the container key must remain the same record: the filter already maps aliases to the same entity set the resolver will now normalize to — prove it with a test for at least "project" and "matter". An unknown route name keeps being denied by the filter; if it ever reaches the resolver it gets the typed refusal, not the "No storage container is configured" 409.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2">Scope: record-less paths. Document-only saves with no related record remain supported; this task changes only calls that NAME an entity. Do not make any target required.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement decision citing bff-extensions.md; publish size against a FRESH master build (short path, same zip tool, both sizes, delta, file counts); at most 60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. No Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration or ctor null-check tests; keep the integration tests at their KEEP path (tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl).</constraint>
  </constraints>

