  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a secure sprk_project, ResolveForRecordAsync("project", id) returns the same ResolvedSecure decision (or the same 409 fail-closed when it has no container) as ResolveForRecordAsync("sprk_project", id); the same holds for "matter"/"sprk_matter" and "workassignment"/"sprk_workassignment".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a non-secure record named by alias, the decision equals the logical-name decision (owning-BU container or caller fallback).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: ResolveForRecordAsync("not_an_entity", id) and ("sprk_projectt", id) throw the new typed SdapProblemException for BOTH overloads, including when a non-secure fallback container is supplied; no decision is returned and no Dataverse record read is attempted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A real non-securable entity (e.g. "sprk_invoice", "contact") resolves exactly as before.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: an entity SET name ("sprk_projects") and an alias from neither `DocumentAssociationMap` nor Dataverse are refused with the typed exception — never mapped silently.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev, read-only): the registry's known-entity set built from the real metadata query contains the three securable roots AND real non-securable entities used by callers (sprk_document, sprk_invoice, sprk_event, sprk_todo, sprk_communication, contact, email), its size is recorded, and the securable subset is unchanged from before the change (exactly the entities carrying sprk_issecure). This proves the "unfiltered entity query returns every entity" premise (`SecurableEntityRegistry.cs:157-158`) that no unit test can — if it is false, every non-securable upload path would be refused.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a metadata query failure propagates (not read as unknown, not as non-securable); an empty metadata answer is not cached.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A cache entry in the previous format (securable names only) is never interpreted as the known-entity set.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AUTHORIZATION: on PUT /api/obo/records/{entity}/{id}/files/{*path} and POST …/upload-session, an alias ("project") authorizes and resolves the SAME record (no misleading "No storage container is configured" 409 for a record whose container is derivable); an unknown entity name is still denied, never uploaded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ExternalProjectDataEndpoints, ComposeService, CommunicationContainerResolver and OfficeService behave unchanged for their existing inputs (their existing tests pass unmodified).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each new guard, when its line is reverted, makes at least one test fail (recorded in the task note).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF unit + integration suites and NetArchTest green; publish size reported per CLAUDE.md §10 and at most 60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: the cases listed above. Anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task note.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>#1038 (peer issue; the Office caller fix ships in PR #1045). Owner round 2 item 7 and the #1038 section of the session27 note (the Related-To lookup shows a systemuser the secure projects they can access; documents inherit secure settings by association — this task is the defense-in-depth half). The resolver's decision logic is provable with the existing registry/resolver test doubles, but the registry's known-entity set depends on a Dataverse behaviour (the unfiltered metadata query returning every entity), so one read-only MANUAL live gate proves it (no Dataverse in CI). Related: task 133 also edits RecordContainerResolver.cs (the stale "/api/external/projects/provision" route text at `:250-254` is 133's, not this task's); task 150 edits its ABSENT branch after this task.</notes>

