    <outcome date="2026-09-30" branch="task/uac-r2-151">
      COMPLETED (code + tests). The resolver normalizes through DocumentAssociationMap.ToLogicalName. For a non-securable
      name it asks the new ISecurableEntityRegistry.IsKnownEntityAsync and throws SdapProblemException
      container_entity_unknown (400) for a non-entity, never returning a decision. The registry keeps the entity names from
      its existing single metadata query, cached with the securable set under sdap:dv:dv-securable-entities:v2 (shape-checked;
      never cached when empty). Gate satisfied (ToLogicalName present on the branch). No escalation trigger fired: no caller
      passes a non-entity/non-alias name; the alias set is as described; and the shared upload client branches on 409 only,
      so a 400 does not collide. Every guard was proven to bite (transcript in notes/task-151-resolver-entity-hardening.md).
      Read-only live gate against spaarkedev1 confirmed the premise: 1,027 entities known, 1,023 returned with empty
      attribute collections, all required entities present. FINDING: the dev securable subset is 4 entities (incl.
      sprk_invoice), not 3. It is unchanged by this task, but the "sprk_invoice is non-securable" premise is false in dev.
      PENDING for the main session: the post-deploy BFF log-line confirmation, the #1038 comment and #1068 close, the
      TASK-INDEX update, and the batch publish-size measurement. No NuGet change.
    </outcome>
    <outcome date="2026-09-30" branch="task/uac-r2-151" kind="review-fixes">
      COMPLETED (verifier findings 1-3). (1) "No second metadata round trip" now holds on a cache MISS too:
      IsSecurableAsync + IsKnownEntityAsync (each fetched the catalog, so a non-securable or unknown name cost TWO
      full-org metadata queries with Redis down) are replaced by ONE ISecurableEntityRegistry.ClassifyEntityAsync
      returning EntitySecurability {NotAnEntity=0, NotSecurable, Securable} from one catalog value; the resolver makes
      one registry call. Pinned by SecurableEntityRegistryTests.OneResolve_WithTheCacheDown_FetchesMetadataExactlyOnce
      (real registry + real resolver, cache down, 5 names). (2) New AssociationTypeLockstepTests: every
      EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType key is a DocumentAssociationMap spelling and is authorized against the
      live-verified entity set (spaarkedev1 read-only EntityDefinitions, 2026-09-30) of the logical name the resolver
      reads; key sets equal both ways. Enumeration via two internal accessors (InternalsVisibleTo, no reflection).
      (3) RecordContainerResolver.NormalizeEntityName documents the alias-wins exception for bare "invoice" (OOB D365
      Sales entity; dev has none, 404); pinned by BareInvoice_ResolvesAsSprkInvoice_EvenWhenTheOrgHasTheOobInvoiceEntity.
      Bites: P1 3 red, P2a 1, P2b 2, P2c 2, P3 2, P4 6; all restored (diff hash identical). Registry doubles
      consolidated on tests/integration/Shared/Dataverse/TestEntityCatalog. Details: notes/task-151-resolver-entity-hardening.md.
    </outcome>
  </execution>
</task>
